4. The Paterine so. This is a special form of the appealing so: In the midst of that aesthetically so brilliant world of Greater Greece is an example. The so is deliberately inserted before a descriptive adjective, & is a way of saying, at once urbanely & concisely, Has it ever occurred to you how brilliant &c. it was? ;
===
4. The Paterine *so*. This is a special form of the appealing *so*: *In the midst of that aesthetically* so *brilliant world of Greater Greece is an example.* The *so* is deliberately inserted before a descriptive adjective, & is a way of saying, at once urbanely & concisely, Has it ever occurred to you how brilliant &c. it was?;
>>>

